{title: We'll Understand It Better By and By}
{artist: Charles Albert Tindley}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
We are [G]tossed and driven on the [C]restless sea of [G]time,
somber skies and howling tempests oft suc[D]ceed a bright sunshine;
in that [G]land of perfect day, when the [C]mists have rolled a[G]way,
we will [D]understand it better by and [G]by.

Chorus
By and [G]by, when the morning comes, when the [C]saints of God are [G]gathered home,
we'll tell the story how we've [D]overcome, for we'll [G]understand it [D]better by and [G]by.
